<title>USA: Tenney, pension fund enter settlement.</title>
<headline>Tenney, pension fund enter settlement.</headline>
<dateline>UNION, N.J. 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tenney Engineering Inc said on Friday it reached a settlement with the Sheet Metal Workers' National Pension Fund over the company's withdrawal liability obligation after it ceased manufacturing at a plant in 1993.</p>
<p>Tenney said it would pay the fund $397,330 plus interest over five years with an initial payment of $75,000.</p>
<p>The payments will be applied against the reserve of $581,835 the company has on its balance sheet and any balance in the reserve will be recognized as the forgiveness of debt when payments are completed, Tenney said.</p>
</text>
